    "issue_alignment": "Issue: 'sess' is not set to NULL after being freed. In tls_decrypt_ticket (ssl/t1_lib.c:1386) SSL_SESSION_free(sess) is followed by goto end without 'sess = NULL', so *psess (line 1476) exposes the freed pointer. tls_parse_ctos_psk then continues its identities loop with a dangling non-NULL sess and calls ssl_session_dup(sess, 0) (line 1110) on the freed object -> use-after-free. PoC: a TLS 1.3 ClientHello with a pre_shared_key extension containing two identities; the first identity is a forged session ticket (fuzzer RNG makes the RFC5077 keys deterministic) that decrypts to a valid SSL_SESSION DER plus one leftover byte, so the slen != 0 branch frees sess without NULLing it."
